1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:03,217
Two words. A whole network, faster.

2
00:00:03,867 --> 00:00:07,112
MISS means the package still
has to come from the mirror.

3
00:00:11,367 --> 00:00:14,392
HIT means it is already in your cache.

4
00:00:14,492 --> 00:00:17,574
And that is exactly what
makes Cache & Carry so handy.

5
00:00:18,867 --> 00:00:21,810
Try it yourself. Open source on GitHub.
